.TH BOSWAS-CP 1 "October 2026" "boswas-control-plane 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-cp \- set up, run and administer the Boswas Control Plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-cp
.RB [ \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR]"
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Boswas Control Plane manages Boswas OS devices: device registry and
enrollment, heartbeats and inventory, typed management commands, signed
device policies, the catalog of 64-bit Windows applications, and an audit
trail. Devices authenticate with certificates (mutual TLS); operators with
API tokens over the HTTPS API and the web dashboard.
.PP
There is no remote shell: commands are typed operations (install, update,
remove, launch, stop and repair an application; refresh the inventory; apply
the policy; update the agent). 32-bit Windows applications are marked
unsupported and are never installed.
.PP
Administration commands work directly on the data directory; run them as the
service user
.B boswas-cp
(or root) on the Control Plane host. Secrets (operator and enrollment tokens)
are printed once and stored only as hashes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "init \-\-public\-url " URL " \-\-server\-name " NAME " " \fR[...] " [\-\-admin " NAME ]
Create the server and device CAs, the TLS server certificate (for the given
DNS names and IP addresses), the Ed25519 policy key, the database, the
default policy and the first administrator, whose API token is printed.
.TP
.B serve
Run the HTTPS API, the dashboard and the background sweeper (systemd unit
.BR boswas-control-plane.service ).
The device port
.RB ( LISTEN_PORT ,
8443) asks for a client certificate and serves enrollment and the device
API; the operator port
.RB ( OPERATOR_LISTEN_PORT ,
9443) never asks for one and serves the dashboard and the operator API.
An endpoint requested on the other port is refused with
.BR WRONG_PORT .
.TP
.BR "operator add " \fINAME\fR " \-\-role viewer" | operator | admin
Create an operator and print its API token. Also
.B operator list
and
.BI "operator disable " NAME .
.TP
.BR "token create " [ \-\-profile " \fIP\fR] [" \-\-policy " \fINAME\fR] [" \-\-ttl\-hours " \fIN\fR] [" \-\-max\-uses " \fIN\fR] [" \-\-allow\-ephemeral "] [" \-\-device " \fIDEVICE_ID\fR]
Create a one-time device enrollment token.
With
.BR \-\-device ,
only that device can use it; this is required to re-enroll a device that is
already enrolled (for example after a reinstallation that kept its ID).
.TP
.BI "artifact add " FILE
Store a Windows installer (.exe or .msi) for catalog applications.
.TP
.BI "catalog add " MANIFEST.json " \fR[\fB\-\-installer \fIFILE\fR]"
Add or replace a catalog application (compatibility manifest format v1; the
manifest must pin its installer's SHA-256). Also
.BR "catalog list" .
.TP
.BI "policy publish " POLICY.json
Publish a new, signed version of a device policy
.RB ( name ", " description ", " compat ", " agent ", " updates ).
Also
.BR "policy list" .
.TP
.BR "device list" " | " "device retire " \fIDEVICE_ID\fR
List devices or retire one (its certificate stops working).
.TP
.BR "events list" " | " "events verify"
Show the audit trail or check its hash chain.
.TP
.B ca\-certificate
Print the CA certificate devices pin
.RB ( CONTROL_PLANE_CA
in
.IR /etc/boswas/device.conf ).
.TP
.B sweep
Mark silent devices offline and expire undelivered commands once.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/boswas\-control\-plane/control\-plane.conf
Configuration (no secrets): device port
.RB ( LISTEN_ADDRESS ", " LISTEN_PORT ", " PUBLIC_URL ),
operator port
.RB ( OPERATOR_LISTEN_ADDRESS ", " OPERATOR_LISTEN_PORT ;
an empty port disables it), data and dashboard directories, limits.
.TP
.I /var/lib/boswas\-control\-plane/
Database, CAs, server and policy keys, stored installers (0700).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas-device (1)
